@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Flow: facility page (client-sessioned utterance)\nConstruct the facility page from free text — triage, scope mining to the page's members, dispatch the facility NUCC filter and Geo in parallel, reconcile on facility_search, respond

actor "Person / Client" as P
participant "Gate\n(facade, transport only)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices main)" as UN
database "Registry\n(the one live map)" as REG
database "Repository\nsessions, ledger, params" as REPO
participant "UtteranceManager\n(classify; RequestUsersRefinement)" as UM
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(FindCare satellite)" as PXY
participant "specialty_filter\n(facility NUCC partition:\nAmbulatory / Psychiatric / Inpatient)" as SF
participant "Geo\n(free-text geography,\nmisspellings)" as GEO
participant "facility_search\n(organizations, NPI Type 2, tool)" as FS

P -> GATE : POST /  { session_token, head,\nparams(utterance, history) }\ne.g. "dialysis centers near Cleveland"
activate GATE
note over GATE
  The gate knows only transport: it collects the token, the HTTP
  head, and the POST/GET params, each if present, and hands them
  on. No routes of its own, verifies nothing.
end note
GATE -> UN : pass(session_token, head, params)
activate UN
deactivate GATE

== Triage: which of the five call types ==
UN -> REG : read the live map for this env
REG --> UN : routes, may_call, pages, required_members
UN -> UN : proof is a session_token ->\ncall_type = client_sessioned\n(five types: tool_to_tool, third_party_callback,\nstatic_witness, client_sessioned, internal_callback)
UN -> REPO : verify token, advance nonce,\nload in-force parameters
REPO --> UN : session ok, params in force
note left of UN
  The UniversalNavigator is the only node that takes external
  traffic. It triages every arrival by its declared proof.
  A bad or missing proof is refused.
end note

== Determine the page and scope mining ==
UN -> UN : this request constructs\npage = facility (NPI Type 2)\nmembers: facility_search, specialty_filter (facility NUCC),\nGeo, facility_detail ; required: facility_search
UN -> UM : classify(utterance, history)\nfragments scoped to facility members
activate UM
UM --> UN : dispatch set { specialty_filter, Geo, facility_search }
deactivate UM
note right of UM
  One model call: cached preamble plus the page members'
  registry fragments in, routes out. Knows no parameters,
  never waits on a tool. The assembled fragments ARE the
  classifier.
end note

== Render ledger: record what the page owes ==
UN -> REPO : record expectation = required_members\n{ facility_search } ; start render_timeout budget
note left of REPO
  Dispatch records the page's required_members as ledger
  expectations. Each completion callback closes one; the
  completeness.render_timeout_seconds budget races them.
end note

== Dispatch: facility NUCC filter and Geo run in parallel ==
par facility NUCC filter -> kinds
  UN -> PXY : dispatch specialty_filter { complaint }\n(satellite, our_signature signed out)
  activate PXY
  PXY -> SF : relay locally (function call)
  activate SF
  SF -> SF : Non-Individual partition; macro-toggles\nAmbulatory / Psychiatric / Inpatient\n(mirrors Prescribers / Homeopathic on the individual page)
  SF --> PXY : { nucc_codes, UserRefinementRequestText }
  deactivate SF
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback { nucc_codes }\nproof: our_signature verified
  deactivate PXY
else Geo -> resolved geography
  UN -> PXY : dispatch Geo { free-text geography }
  activate PXY
  PXY -> GEO : relay locally (function call)
  activate GEO
  GEO -> GEO : resolve "Cleveland" (incl. misspellings)\n-> state / place (recursion-guarded)
  GEO --> PXY : { geography, UserRefinementRequestText }
  deactivate GEO
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback { geography }\nproof: our_signature verified
  deactivate PXY
end
note over SF, FS
  Every tool output carries UserRefinementRequestText:
  populated = the tool is ASKING the user (the UtteranceManager
  delivers it via RequestUsersRefinement(question));
  empty = the tool is answering.
end note
UN -> REPO : merge serially (deterministic);\na state conflict RAISES

== Dispatch the required member ==
alt geography is sufficient
  UN -> PXY : dispatch facility_search\n{ nucc_codes, geography }
  activate PXY
  PXY -> FS : relay locally (function call)
  activate FS
  FS -> FS : match organizations only, active,\nby name / taxonomy / practice-location\ngeography / administrator (recursion-guarded)
  FS --> PXY : { rows, total, UserRefinementRequestText }
  deactivate FS
  PXY --> UN : internal_callback { rows }\nproof: our_signature verified
  deactivate PXY
  alt required member closes within render_timeout_seconds
    UN -> REPO : close facility_search entry;\nserial merge (conflict RAISES)
    UN -> UN : page reconciled -\nrequired_members all closed
  else render_timeout budget expires first
    UN -> UN : ledger race lost -> layman on_timeout\nexplanation (instrumented, timings)
  end
else geography insufficient - required input unmet
  UN -> UM : RequestUsersRefinement()\nmissing slot: geography { in-force, utterance }
  activate UM
  UM -> UM : own LLM authors\none user-facing sentence
  UM --> UN : one user-facing sentence
  deactivate UM
  note right of UM
    RequestUsersRefinement lives only inside the UtteranceManager — the one
    conversational surface; no tool ever talks to the user directly. Two forms:
    * RequestUsersRefinement()          -> the UM's own LLM authors the question
                                           (no dispatchable route / missing slot, as here)
    * RequestUsersRefinement(question)  -> the UM delivers a question a dispatched tool
                                           authored (its UserRefinementRequestText populated)
  end note
end

note over UN, REPO
  Page error management, all instrumented with timings at a
  severity matching impact:
  * timeout  -> respond with the layman on_timeout explanation
  * parameter / state merge conflict -> RAISE
  * a required member that dies or never calls back -> RAISE
  Every throw ends in a UniversalNavigator; the proxy re-raises.
end note

UN -> GATE : stream the merged answer, sequenced\n(the gate owns the one stream)
activate GATE
GATE -> P : the one stream the gate writes
deactivate GATE
deactivate UN

note over REG
  Registry drift footnote: the built registry instance
  (build 2292) does not yet list the facility NUCC filter
  member; this flow depicts the current iteration, which adds it.
end note

@enduml
